{"name":"Winter Wonderland","hex":"#b3bfc8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winter wonderland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beautiful scene of snow and ice.","A festive funfair held around Christmas time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winter_wonderland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winter Wonderland","blocks":[{"text":"\"Winter Wonderland\" is a song written in 1934 by Felix Bernard and lyricist Richard Bernhard Smith. Due to its seasonal theme, it is commonly regarded as a Christmas song in the Northern Hemisphere. Since its original recording by Richard Himber, it has been covered by over 200 different artists. Its lyrics are about a couple's romance during winter."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Winter_Wonderland_sheet_music.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_Wonderland","wikidata":"Q195814"},{"title":"Winter wonderland","blocks":[{"text":"A winter wonderland or Christmas fair is the catch all name for a funfair held mainly in the United Kingdom around the Christmas season. A winter wonderland usually includes attractions such as a German-style Christmas market, Santa's grotto, amusement rides and ice skating rinks. Winter wonderlands range from small-scale single-day events to large city centre fairs lasting several weeks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Winter_Wonderland%2C_Hyde_Park%2C_London_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4749324.jpg/330px-Winter_Wonderland%2C_Hyde_Park%2C_London_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4749324.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_wonderland","wikidata":"Q126001934"},{"title":"Winter","blocks":[{"text":"Winter is the coldest and darkest season of the year in temperate and polar climates. It occurs after autumn and before spring, when the hemisphere is oriented away from the Sun as a result of the tilt of Earth's axis. Different cultures define different dates as the start of winter, and some use a definition based on weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/330px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter","wikidata":"Q1311"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Open-air_Skating_in_Princes_Street_Gardens_-_geograph.org.uk_-_919864.jpg/500px-Open-air_Skating_in_Princes_Street_Gardens_-_geograph.org.uk_-_919864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Open-air_Skating_in_Princes_Street_Gardens_-_geograph.org.uk_-_919864.jpg/500px-Open-air_Skating_in_Princes_Street_Gardens_-_geograph.org.uk_-_919864.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ice skating at Princes Street Gardens in 2000, a precursor to the Edinburgh's Christmas wonderland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOpen-air_Skating_in_Princes_Street_Gardens_-_geograph.org.uk_-_919864.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Matcham%27s_Park%2C_barrels_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1198604.jpg/500px-Matcham%27s_Park%2C_barrels_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1198604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Matcham%27s_Park%2C_barrels_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1198604.jpg/500px-Matcham%27s_Park%2C_barrels_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1198604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The poor quality of Lapland New Forest made the site notorious as a \"winter blunderland\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatcham's_Park%2C_barrels_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1198604.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thu